---

## 7. Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| UI Framework | SwiftUI | Native iOS, declarative, Universal (iPhone + iPad) |
| Language | Swift 5.9+ | Modern, safe, Apple-native |
| Database + Auth | Supabase (supabase-swift SDK) | PostgreSQL, built-in auth, RLS, free tier |
| Payments | Razorpay iOS SDK | India-focused, easy integration, test mode available |
| Architecture | MVVM | SwiftUI standard, clean separation |
| Minimum Target | iOS 16+ | Broad device support, modern SwiftUI features |
| Device Support | Universal (iPhone + iPad) | Maximum reach |
| Distribution | Xcode Simulator (dev) | No Apple Developer Account |

---

## 8. Demo Scenario

```
1. User opens DonateNow app on iPhone/iPad
2. Views the cause with title, description, and progress
3. Selects ₹500 as donation amount
4. Fills in name and email
5. Taps "Donate Now"
6. Completes payment via Razorpay Checkout (iOS)
7. Thank-you screen is displayed with donation details
8. Admin logs into admin section within the app
9. Admin sees the ₹500 donation in the donor log
```

---

## 9. Success Criteria

- [ ] Payment flow works successfully in test mode
- [ ] Thank-you screen is displayed after donation
- [ ] Admin can view the donor log

---

## 10. Constraints

- MVP scope only — no recurring donations, no receipt generation, no multi-cause support
- Test mode only — no real money processed during development
- Single admin role — no role hierarchy
- No Apple Developer Account — Xcode Simulator distribution only
- iOS only — no Android, no web
- No push notifications in MVP

